AB  - Risks and benefits of vegetarianism and veganism. Vegetarianism, dietary veganism and veganism reduce the risk of developing type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease or stroke, metabolic syndrome and even certain cancers. However, these diets do present risks if they are poorly conducted. It is necessary to prevent deficiencies in vitamins B12 and D, iron, iodine, calcium, zinc and omega-3. The pharmacist should accompany people who wish to adopt this type of diet and advise them on useful food supplements. (c) 2020 Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved
